repos/P-A-R-U-S/Go-Job-Worker-Service/pulls/2","html_url":"https://github.com/P-A-R-U-S/Go-Job-Worker-Service/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/P-A-R-U-S/Go-Job-Worker-Service/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/P-A-R-U-S/Go-Job-Worker-Service/pull/2.patch","merged_at":"2024-09-09T23:23:17Z"},"body":"PR contains implements for library that running arbitrary Linux 64-bit process in isolation with resource limits. For details, please, follow this RFD Document: https://github.com/P-A-R-U-S/Go-Job-Worker-Service/blob/library/docs/RFD-JobWorkerService.md\r\n\r\nTo run test you can use following make command:\r\n\r\n* `make run_test_cgroup` - run sunset of tests for cgroups\r\n* `make run_test_output` - run subset of test for OutputReader and all related to Steam command output\r\n* `make run_test_job` - run sunset of tests for Job executing (you can check Test Plan section in RFD Document)\r\n\r\n_**Note**: because `make run_test_job` need to create and manages crgoup, you possibly need [sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) permission to run tests._\r\n\r\nPackage structure and files name are self-explained, but here is some details: \r\n\r\n```\r\n |-Makefile (\r\n |-pkg\r\n | |-jobWorker\r\n | | |-namespaces\r\n | | | |-cgroup.go               --> constains all cgroup functions\r\n | | | |-cgroup_test.go\r\n | | | |-mount.go\r\n | | |-job.go              --> contains all Start/Stop/Stream/Status implementation\r\n | | |-job_test.go\r\n | | |-outputReadCloser.go      --> implements io.ReadCloser interface to read from the provided CommandOutput\r\n | | |-outputReadCloser_test.go\r\n | | |-commandOutput.go               --> implements io.Closer and io.Writer and implement a command buffer\r\n | | |-commandOutput_test.go\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"P-A-R-U-S","id":1575452,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzU0NTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1575452?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/P-A-R-U-S","html_url":"https: